# Build context is the repo root (monorepo Dockerfiles). Keep it lean:
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.data
*.local
.git
.github
apps/driver
docs
**/*.md
# Foundry project — never COPY'd by apps/web/Dockerfile, and `out/` alone is
# megabytes of build context uploaded for nothing on every deploy.
contracts
# Real private keys live in apps/web/.env.market. Only .gitignore was keeping
# them out of the image, which does nothing for a local `docker build` — those
# keys would be baked into an intermediate layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*
